{"reasoning": "Criterion GO002 requires: (1) three cities with daily rate matching by county and season, (2) correct FY2025/FY2026 mapping, and (3) original table row numbers for both years.\n\nVerification:\n- Chicago: FY2025 (Sep 28-30) \u2192 row 258 (Cook/Lake, Sep 1-Sep 30, lodging 223, M&IE 92); FY2026 (Oct 1-2) \u2192 row 254 (Cook/Lake, Oct 1-Nov 30, lodging 223, M&IE 92). Matches source files exactly.\n- Denver: FY2025 (Sep 28-30) \u2192 row 109 (Denver/Adams/Arapahoe/Jefferson, Apr 1-Sep 30, lodging 215, M&IE 92); FY2026 (Oct 1-2) \u2192 row 107 (same county, Oct 1-Oct 31, lodging 215, M&IE 92). Matches source files exactly.\n- Phoenix: FY2025 (Sep 28-30) \u2192 row 22 (Maricopa, Sep 1-Sep 30, lodging 160, M&IE 86); FY2026 (Oct 1-2) \u2192 row 18 (Maricopa, Oct 1-Jan 31, lodging 160, M&IE 86). Matches source files exactly.\n\nRow numbers are provided in the Daily sheet's `excel_row` column and in the Sources sheet (listing rows per city per FY). The approval_brief.docx references \"\u539f\u8868\u884c\u53f7\u89c1Daily/Sources\". All three deliverables are consistent. Season/county matching is correct for all 15 daily entries.", "score": "yes"}

